WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.252
AI is smart.

00:00:02.292 --> 00:00:04.363
But the way we use it?

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:07.128
It's frustratingly dumb.

00:00:07.168 --> 00:00:09.415
It doesn't know what's new.

00:00:09.455 --> 00:00:12.817
It rewrites code that already exists.

00:00:12.857 --> 00:00:16.787
And it has trouble with long-horizon tasks.

00:00:17.226 --> 00:00:20.987
Bigger models alone won't fix this.

00:00:21.027 --> 00:00:26.993
Teleion Fabric is a fabric of OmniNodes that keeps evolving.

00:00:27.405 --> 00:00:33.453
It reconfigures itself for each Task, to run it the best way.

00:00:34.753 --> 00:00:39.131
Meta's Muse models help power the fabric.

00:00:39.202 --> 00:00:45.079
A small Meta-based decider helps pick the model for real Tasks.

00:00:45.148 --> 00:00:49.979
A fine-tuned Meta model helps improve performance.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:53.905
Meta models run through several routes.

00:00:53.945 --> 00:00:58.656
It can adapt and use new models as they come out.

00:00:58.696 --> 00:01:04.401
It keeps learning from new events, code reuse and long tasks.

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:08.777
Long work becomes small Tasks in a queue.

00:01:08.817 --> 00:01:14.296
Finished work stays as Task Objects the next agent reuses.

00:01:14.862 --> 00:01:17.260
Every run is recorded.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:21.730
Over time, it learns which models and workers fit which Tasks,

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:25.882
and when deterministic code is the right choice.

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:31.214
In our testing, a repeated job used far fewer tokens.

00:01:31.346 --> 00:01:34.554
One run needed no model at all.

00:01:35.405 --> 00:01:37.496
And we measure it.

00:01:37.536 --> 00:01:44.345
Correct answers about new GitHub projects went from 0 to 26 of 30.

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:49.806
In our testing, it wrote about 16 percent less code.

00:01:50.238 --> 00:01:56.657
When a crash hit, the whole job took 7 model calls, not 10.

00:01:57.393 --> 00:02:01.024
And this is running right now.

00:02:02.929 --> 00:02:09.526
Teleion Fabric can run almost anything, and we decided to put it to work, with Eranos.

00:02:09.566 --> 00:02:15.913
A nonprofit presses My NGO needs help, and says what it needs.

00:02:15.953 --> 00:02:20.603
It can be a cited report, or a reusable process.

00:02:20.643 --> 00:02:25.422
Agents pick up the work, one small Task at a time.

00:02:25.837 --> 00:02:32.527
Anyone with spare AI can press I want to help, and connect their agent.

00:02:32.759 --> 00:02:39.096
The team decides what to use, and every solution joins a free library.

00:02:39.262 --> 00:02:44.140
See it at eranosforgood.org.

00:02:44.431 --> 00:02:47.916
Open one.

00:02:47.963 --> 00:02:51.086
Press Adapt it for my group.

00:02:51.921 --> 00:02:54.019
AI is smart.

00:02:54.059 --> 00:02:57.445
Now the way we use it can be smart too.

00:02:57.485 --> 00:02:59.700
Connect your agents today.

